      "body": "### Neovim version (nvim -v)\n\n0.7.2\n\n### Vim (not Nvim) behaves the same?\n\nyes, 8.2.4113\n\n### Operating system/version\n\nmacOS 12.4\n\n### Terminal name/version\n\nTerminal.app 2.12.7\n\n### $TERM environment variable\n\nscreen-256color\n\n### Installation\n\nhomebrew\n\n### How to reproduce the issue\n\nAll in default macos Terminal.app\r\n\r\nSetup tmux configs following `:checkhealth` recommendations, like:\r\n```tmux\r\nset-option -g default-terminal \"screen-256color\"\r\nset-option -sa terminal-overrides ',xterm-256color:RGB' # 'cause xterm-256color is $TERM outside of tmux\r\n```\r\n\r\nSetup nvim `termguicolors` as true\r\n\r\nReload tmux and nvim\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nNo warnings while `:checkhealth` for Terminal.app($TERM == xterm-256color) + tmux ($TERM screen-256color) runtime environment\n\n### Actual behavior\n\nThere are either warning with actual colors or nothing warn but broken color support\r\n<img width=\"1471\" alt=\"\u0421\u043d\u0438\u043c\u043e\u043a \u044d\u043a\u0440\u0430\u043d\u0430 2022-06-30 \u0432 21 12 00\" src=\"https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/33671815/176752468-951e6a8c-c19f-4868-a358-4e7a06bcf96a.png\">\r\n<img width=\"1680\" alt=\"\u0421\u043d\u0438\u043c\u043e\u043a \u044d\u043a\u0440\u0430\u043d\u0430 2022-06-30 \u0432 21 14 10\" src=\"https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/33671815/176752886-50dee255-3000-4b7a-b171-17da42f1dc7d.png\">",
